course: dictionary
lesson: 1336
title: The word camera
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A camera is a device for taking photographs or making videos. You can find one in a phone, a tablet or a computer, or fixed to a wall to watch an area, like a security camera. «The camera showed Jamie — and Ben standing right next to him.» The camera recorded what happened, so it showed the truth.
explain: Think of how a camera works. Light goes through a lens and makes an image, a bit like your eye does. That is why a camera can capture a picture of something, even when you are not there to see it.
explain: Words can have more than one meaning in different places. «On camera» means being filmed, so a person who is on camera is being recorded. In online safety, think before you take or share photos, and ask people before you photograph them.
fact: A camera is a device for taking photographs or making videos.
fact: A camera can be part of a phone, tablet or computer, or fixed to watch an area, like a security camera.
fact: In a camera, light goes through a lens and makes an image, a bit like an eye.
fact: «On camera» means being filmed.
fact: Before digital cameras, photos were taken on film, and a roll often had only 24 or 36 pictures.
exercise: «The camera showed Jamie — and Ben standing right next to him.» What is a camera? | A bell on a bicycle | *A device for taking photographs or making videos | A tall tree in a park | A kind of lens for glasses
exercise: Which of these can be a camera? | A teaspoon | *A phone | A wooden chair | A cushion
exercise: Why do scientists use camera photos of tigers? | *To tell them apart by their stripes | To cook them a meal | To count their teeth | To make them into a film about cooking
test: «On camera» means | being hungry | *being filmed | being in a dark room | being very quiet
test: In a camera, light goes through a | cupboard | sock | puddle | *lens
exam: Which is a safe rule about photos? | Keep webcams on when talking to strangers | Share every photo with strangers online | *Ask people before you photograph them | Take photos of everyone you meet
